## Disposition

Retain the proposal’s reader / project-database / viewer-adapter architecture as a bounded prototype direction. The document correctly separates source samples from display state, makes calibration and provenance explicit, limits initial formats, gives a useful recovery model, and marks whole-application behavior as unverified. Its OME/TIFF, tifffile, napari, SQLite, and Bio-Formats claims are mostly scoped appropriately.

Three design contracts need to be made explicit before implementation: (1) a stable content identity for directory stores such as OME-Zarr; (2) bounded, transactional storage and undo for potentially large masks; and (3) one precise coordinate convention spanning sample centers, pixel edges, pyramid levels, viewer coordinates, and exported geometry. The proposal already identifies the center/corner risk; the open napari issue makes that a release gate. SQLite transactions also cover the database, not the database plus image/mask/export files, so recovery needs a cross-file operation protocol.

This is a correction review, not a claim that the components have been integrated or qualified. I performed no code execution or application test. The inherited witness W1 is labeled **executed by candidate** in the research catalog; its receipt checks supplied arithmetic only. Research checks P1–P6 remain **proposed/UNEXECUTED**. No evaluator check is present.

